          "text": "ECG demonstrated T-wave inversion in V4-6 and troponin rose from 287 to 412, with a high-risk GRACE score. Creatinine was 168 on Day 2 (13/05), improving to 142 by Day 4 (15/05). Inpatient coronary angiogram confirmed severe three-vessel disease not suitable for PCI; following MDT review, medical management was agreed. Dual antiplatelet therapy was commenced with ticagrelor, fondaparinux was started, bisoprolol was uptitrated to 7.5mg once daily, and isosorbide mononitrate 30mg once daily was added. She mobilised with physiotherapy and a cardiac rehabilitation referral was completed.",
